onal system which is  called ctas that's been completely  switched off now  um so we no longer have access to that  and test and trace support payments they  ended from the 24th of february  and but anybody who tested positive  before that they still have 42 days to  claim that testing trade support payment  which takes us up to the 23rd of april  so if anybody tested positive before the  24th of february they still have 42 days  to claim  um the national team are reviewing the  kovic capability across local  authorities if we do need to step things  back up so that's a piece of work that's  been undertaken  and and obviously as a local authority  we're developing processes and systems  if we do need to step things back up  quickly  um all our businesses and schools know  that we're here to support them in an  outbreak situation and we just continue  to offer advice and guidance to them  thank you thank you kirsty that's very  reassuring and and i think  as a school chair of governors i know  how good the the the outbreak  management's been with schools and and  you know and the schools of my school  where it's happened it has been really  really impressed so thank you very very  much indeed are there any questions at  all uh for kirsty  i don't see any kirstie can i thank you  for your contributions to these meetings  it's been very very informative thank  you  uh can i therefore invite benice to talk  to us about uh care outbreaks and care  homes and assisted living denise welcome  thank you good morning chair  over the past week we have been seeing  increased activity across our care homes  and supported accommodation settings  we have  three settings uh on our watch list at  the moment and eight settings with an  outbreak and we have managed to close  around 16 outbreaks since january  we have we continue to work very closely  with our settings um together  information on any cases that are  identified  see if there's any ongoing transmission  within our setting